course: dictionary
lesson: 4322
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them tell you which meaning the writer wants. A grower is a person, a company, a plant or even a song, so you need the clues to pick the right one. «Ukraine is one of the world's biggest sunflower growers and sells more sunflower oil than any other country.» Here the sunflower growers are farmers who grow sunflowers to sell, because the sentence is about selling oil.
explain: «Bumblebees shake tomato flowers to release their pollen, and greenhouse growers keep boxes of bumblebees to pollinate tomatoes.» Greenhouse growers are the people who grow tomatoes in greenhouses. Check it by putting your meaning into the sentence: people who grow tomatoes in greenhouses keep bumblebees. That makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Now look at a different meaning. Sam says, «That song's a grower.» The song is not growing and nobody is growing it. The word means a song you do not like at first but come to like more and more each time you hear it. Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence.
fact: A grower is a person or company that grows plants, fruit or vegetables to sell.
fact: A fruit grower or a flower grower is someone who grows fruit or flowers.
fact: A grower can also be a plant that grows in a certain way, such as «a fast grower» or «a slow grower».
fact: In informal talk, «a grower» is a song, show or thing you do not like at first but come to like more and more.
fact: To check a meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Ukraine is one of the world's biggest sunflower growers.» What is a sunflower grower? | *A person or company that grows sunflowers to sell | A yellow flower on a windowsill | A bee that visits sunflowers | A machine that makes sunflower oil
exercise: «Greenhouse growers keep boxes of bumblebees to pollinate tomatoes.» What does greenhouse growers mean here? | Bees that live in greenhouses | Children who water the plants | Boxes that keep bees warm | *People who grow tomatoes and other plants in greenhouses
exercise: Mia says, «My bean is a fast grower.» What does a fast grower mean? | A bean that runs very fast | *A plant that grows quickly | A bean that is ready to eat today | A gardener who is always in a hurry
test: Sam says, «That song's a grower, and I like it more each time I hear it.» What is a grower here? | *A song you come to like more and more | A tune played on a flute | A person who writes songs | A singer who sings in a choir
test: «A fruit grower sells apples at the market.» What is a fruit grower? | A fruit that grows very big | A person who eats fruit every day | *A person who grows fruit to sell | A shopkeeper who sells fruit
exam: Which phrase means a plant that grows quickly? | a wheat grower | a flower grower | a grower of sunflower oil | *a fast grower
